  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.553,
            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Baudhāyana-Pythagoras Theorem"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.086,
            0.831,
            0.111
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why is PQRS a square? Why is its area half that of the original paper?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.112,
            0.844,
            0.152
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Explain by connecting QS and PR, finding the different angles formed, and then using tringle congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.174,
            0.772,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.3 Hypotenuse of an Isosceles Right Triangle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.207,
            0.845,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall that in a right triangle, the side opposite to the right angle is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "hypotenuse.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.256,
            0.647,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Find the hypotenuse of this isosceles right triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.282,
            0.692,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that a square of side 1 unit is made of two such isosceles right triangles. We also know that the square constructed on the diagonal of this square has twice the area of the original square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.702,
            0.248,
            0.855,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.702,
                0.248,
                0.855,
                0.359
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.362,
            0.648,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.375,
                0.362,
                0.648,
                0.579
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.587,
            0.845,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We do not yet know the length of the hypotenuse, but we know the area of the square REST on it!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.629,
            0.657,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of REST = 2 × Area of PEAR"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.47,
            0.659,
            0.663,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "= 2 × 1 = 2 sq. units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.683,
            0.846,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know the relation between the side and the area of a square. If c is the hypotenuse ER, then"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.34,
            0.725,
            0.578,
            0.744
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Area}   of  \\mathrm{REST} = c \\times c = c^{2}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.416,
            0.749,
            0.511,
            0.768
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\scriptstyle { \\mathrm { S } } 0 ,   c ^ { 2 } \\; = \\; 2 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.772,
            0.527,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = { \\sqrt { 2 } } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.798,
            0.567,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the hypotenuse is of length "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
